# Fusion Equilibrium Challenge entry — CITATION.cff

cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Fusion Equilibrium Challenge: the Anulum entry"
message: "If you use this code, the trained model or the experiment record, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Šotek"
    given-names: "Miroslav"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-3560-0851"
    email: "protoscience@anulum.li"
    affiliation: "ANULUM / Fortis Studio"
abstract: >-
  Reproduction package and experiment record of an entry to the Fusion Equilibrium Challenge (NeurIPS 2026
  competition): reconstruction of tokamak flux maps, q95 and normalised beta from coil currents and
  Thomson-scattering profiles without magnetic measurements. An ensemble of multilayer perceptrons with
  tree-based and specialist heads and a map-finishing step for DIII-D, and an equal-temperature free-boundary
  reconstruction for MAST without any MAST training data. Developed with Arcane Sapience, the entrant's
  research system built on large language models.
keywords:
  - tokamak
  - plasma equilibrium
  - Grad-Shafranov
  - DIII-D
  - MAST
  - machine learning
